1. SYLLABUS AUTHORITY
   ============================================================

The uploaded JAMB/UTME Use of English syllabus is the primary curriculum source for this curriculum.

The supplied syllabus identifies three major sections:

SECTION A — COMPREHENSION AND SUMMARY

SECTION B — LEXIS AND STRUCTURE

SECTION C — ORAL FORMS

The syllabus states that the overall objectives include helping candidates communicate effectively in written and spoken English and use English Language for learning at tertiary level.

Do not silently add unrelated English Language topics simply because they appear in general secondary-school English textbooks.

Every proposed curriculum item must be classified as:

* CORE JAMB
* SUPPORTING / PREREQUISITE
* APPLICATION
* OPTIONAL / ENRICHMENT
* VERIFY CURRENT JAMB SCOPE
* OUTSIDE JAMB SCOPE

If a concept is not clearly supported by the syllabus:

DO NOT present it as definitely examinable.

Mark it:

"VERIFY CURRENT JAMB SCOPE"

Do not falsely claim that a topic is officially examinable unless it has been verified.

