3. EXAMINATION STRUCTURE
========================

The supplied syllabus specifies a 60-question examination structure:

SECTION A — COMPREHENSION AND SUMMARY

* 1 comprehension passage — 5 questions
* 1 summary passage — 5 questions
* 1 cloze passage — 10 questions
* 1 reading text — 5 questions

SECTION B — LEXIS AND STRUCTURE

* Sentence interpretation — 5 questions
* Antonyms — 5 questions
* Synonyms — 5 questions
* Basic Grammar — 10 questions

SECTION C — ORAL FORMS

* Vowels — 2 questions
* Consonants — 2 questions
* Rhymes — 2 questions
* Word Stress — 2 questions
* Emphatic Stress — 2 questions

TOTAL — 60 QUESTIONS

Use this structure when designing assessment distributions and examination simulations.

Do not claim that every future JAMB examination will necessarily contain exactly the same distribution unless the current official examination structure has been verified.

