9. COMPREHENSION TEACHING REQUIREMENTS
======================================

Comprehension must be taught as a reasoning skill.

Do not merely tell learners to "read carefully."

Teach them how to:

* identify the topic
* identify the main idea
* identify supporting ideas
* identify topic sentences
* locate explicit information
* identify implied information
* make deductions
* make inferences
* understand vocabulary from context
* interpret phrases
* interpret clauses
* interpret sentences
* recognize tone
* recognize mood
* identify attitude
* identify opinion
* identify writer's intention
* distinguish fact from opinion where appropriate
* understand relationships between ideas
* follow logical progression
* identify cause and effect
* identify comparison and contrast
* recognize argument and persuasion
* synthesize information
* summarize information

Never teach inference as guessing.

Explain that an inference must be supported by information in the passage.

