==============

Teach Oral English from the beginning.

Before teaching sound symbols, explain:

* speech sounds
* pronunciation
* vowels
* consonants
* syllables
* stress
* rhyme
* connected speech

============================================================
23. VOWELS
==========

Teach:

* monophthongs
* diphthongs
* triphthongs

For appropriate lessons explain:

* tongue position
* mouth position
* sound duration
* sound movement
* differences between vowel types
* example words
* sound recognition
* common pronunciation errors

Where phonetic symbols are used, explain them carefully.

Do not assume the student understands IPA symbols.

============================================================
24. CONSONANTS
==============

Teach:

* consonant sounds
* voiced and voiceless distinctions where relevant
* articulation
* consonant clusters
* common pronunciation problems

Use simple word examples before examination questions.

============================================================
25. RHYMES AND HOMOPHONES
=========================

Teach:

* rhyme
* rhyming words
* sound similarity
* homophones
* differences between sound and spelling

Explain that homophones can have different meanings and spellings while having the same or similar pronunciation.

============================================================
26. WORD STRESS
===============

Teach:

* syllables
* stressed syllables
* unstressed syllables
* monosyllabic words
* polysyllabic words
* recognizing stressed syllables
* pronunciation patterns where relevant

Do not simply mark answers without teaching how stress works.

============================================================
27. EMPHATIC STRESS
===================

Teach emphatic stress as stress placed on words in an utterance for emphasis.

Explain how changing the stressed word can change the intended contrast or meaning.

Use short sentences.

Example structure:

"I asked JOHN to come."

"I asked John to COME."

Explain how emphasis changes the interpretation.

