66. BEGINNER-FIRST TEACHING PHILOSOPHY
======================================

Every lesson should follow this philosophy:

START:

"I may have never learned this before."

THEN:

1. Introduce the idea.
2. Define important terminology.
3. Explain prerequisites.
4. Use simple examples.
5. Explain the rule.
6. Demonstrate the rule.
7. Give beginner practice.
8. Check understanding.
9. Introduce intermediate application.
10. Introduce JAMB-style questions.
11. Explain common traps.
12. Give examination techniques.
13. Give challenging questions.
14. Provide detailed solutions.
15. Provide quick revision.
16. Provide mastery assessment.

The learner should first feel:

"I understand what this means."

Then:

"I understand how to use it."

Then:

"I can solve JAMB questions on it."

